{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline (generation-run44) for the go-unix-utils project. Task #5224 is a stitch task that requires implementing specific Go utility requirements. The task was created by the measure phase, which analyzed the codebase and selected requirements to implement. The intent is to implement the assigned requirements following the extensive execution constitution, coding standards, and go style constitution provided in the prompt. The task follows a strict workflow: review context → plan approach → implement → verify acceptance criteria. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - no git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries (g-prefixed: gcat, gls, etc.)\n   - cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for verification\n   - SIGPIPE handler (sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler) required for all cmd/ utilities writing to stdout\n   - exec.LookPath + t.Skip pattern for graceful handling of missing reference binaries\n   - 40-line function size limit (hard limit per E8)\n   - 500-line file size limit per E9\n   - DRY enforcement at two-occurrence threshold per E10\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - Write all source files before building/testing (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n   - LC_ALL=C for all differential tests\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` (first 100 lines read)\n     - Contains requirement statuses for all SRDs\n     - srd001-testutils: R1.1-R1.4 complete (issue 5067)